course: dictionary
lesson: 12355
title: Money words: creditworthiness
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Creditworthiness is a long word, so break it into pieces. Credit is money you borrow and promise to pay back later. Worthy means deserving. The ending -ness turns it into a noun, a thing you can name. Together, creditworthiness is how much someone deserves to be trusted with borrowed money.
explain: «The bank checked Mum's creditworthiness before it agreed to lend her money for a new car.» The bank wanted to know one thing: does Mum usually pay back what she owes? Use the clues around the word. Lend and money tell you this is about borrowing, and the bank checking it tells you it is about trust.
explain: A «credit score» is a number that measures creditworthiness. Paying bills on time builds it up, and missed payments damage it. So if you read «Dad's credit score went down after he missed two payments», you can work out that his creditworthiness went down too.
fact: Creditworthiness is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say «good creditworthiness», not «a creditworthiness».
fact: «Creditworthiness» means how safe a bank or shop thinks it is to lend money to a person or company.
fact: Creditworthiness is based on whether someone usually pays back what they owe.
fact: A «credit score» is a number that measures creditworthiness.
fact: Paying bills on time builds creditworthiness; missed payments damage it.
exercise: «Banks check creditworthiness before they lend money.» What does creditworthiness mean? | How fast a person can run to the bank | How much money a shop makes in one day | *How safe a bank thinks it is to lend money to someone | How many coins are in a purse
exercise: A «credit score» is a number. What does it measure? | Speed | Rainfall | *Creditworthiness | Height
exercise: Which habit builds creditworthiness? | *Paying bills on time | Never opening the post | Hiding bills in a drawer | Missing payments
test: «Missed payments damage creditworthiness.» Does a missed payment make creditworthiness better or worse? | Stays exactly the same | *Worse | Better | It has no effect at all
test: Which sentence uses creditworthiness correctly? | *The shop judged his creditworthiness before offering him a card. | She creditworthinessed the bread. | The creditworthiness were very tall. | Creditworthiness is a sunny day at the beach.
exam: Which word means how safe a bank thinks it is to lend money? | Generosity | *Creditworthiness | Curiosity | Friendliness
